Event loop tests
================

Behaviour tests for QEventLoop: timers, posted events, socket notifiers,
nested loops, cross-thread wake-ups, X11 event handling and the
coexistence with GLib sources (GDBus, g_idle_add, g_main_loop_run,
GTask, libpulse's GLib main loop). They were written to compare the
stock select() loop with the GLib based loop (configure -glib-eventloop)
and are not part of the normal build ("make" does not touch this
directory; there is no .pro file on purpose).

Build against the library of this source tree (configure + make first),
or against another tree with QTDIR=...:

    tests/eventloop/build.sh            # in tests/eventloop/build
    tests/eventloop/build.sh -asan      # -fsanitize=address,undefined
    tests/eventloop/build.sh -asan-loop # and the library's event loop
                                        # sources, so that a use after
                                        # free in the loop is caught
    QTDIR=/other/qt tests/eventloop/build.sh build-other

Run everything (the GUI checks only if $DISPLAY is set; run.sh sets
ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0 unless ASAN_OPTIONS is set, because Qt 3
leaks a little on purpose, and the moc of an ASan build of the whole
library needs the same when build.sh runs it):

    tests/eventloop/run.sh [builddir]

or single programs:

    looptest            the main suite (non-GUI)
    looptest gui        the main suite plus the X11 checks; opens a
                        few small windows that close by themselves
    looptest recreate [gui]
                        QApplication destroyed, the GLib main context
                        iterated, a new QApplication created (3 rounds)
    looptest early [gui]
                        QEventLoop created before the QApplication
    looptest workerfirst [before] [gui]
                        another thread uses the event loop before
                        exec() (wakeUpGuiThread(), ...) or, with
                        "before", before the QApplication exists
    looptest cpu [s [gui]]
                        CPU used by a 10 ms QTimer (getrusage)
    t2                  GLib main context iterated after ~QApplication

looptest prints one PASS/FAIL/SKIP line per check and exits with 1 if a
check failed. The program finds out at run time which loop the library
runs (whether the GUI thread owns the default GLib context), so one
binary can be run against both builds of the library:

    LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/path/to/select-loop/lib tests/eventloop/run.sh

Checks that need the GLib loop (GLib and GDBus sources, notifiers on fds
above FD_SETSIZE, ...) are reported as SKIP with the select() loop,
which must pass all the others. The FD_SETSIZE check is also skipped if
the hard RLIMIT_NOFILE is below 1600. For the GUI checks without
disturbing the desktop, use a private X server, e.g.
"Xephyr :37 -screen 1024x768 &" and DISPLAY=:37.

Needs: g++, pkg-config, GLib/GIO development files (gio-2.0), libX11,
a D-Bus session bus for the GDBus checks and, optionally,
libpulse-mainloop-glib with a running PulseAudio/PipeWire server.

Note: <gio/gio.h> (and other GObject headers) must be included before
the Qt headers, because Qt 3 #defines "signals" and GDBusInterfaceInfo
has a member of that name.
